BINARY GATE COLLISIONS
========================================================================
Positive unordered x+y=xy collisions below 40: [(2, 2, 4)]
  Rearrangement: (x-1)(y-1)=1, so the only positive collision is (2,2)->4.

Two-factor product-sum layer by total arity k:
  r ones plus a,b>1 solve r+a+b=ab with k=r+2
  equivalently (a-1)(b-1)=k-1, so this layer is the divisor graph of k-1.
  k= 2: 2,2->P=4
  k= 3: 2,3->P=6
  k= 4: 2,4->P=8
  k= 5: 2,5->P=10, 3,3->P=9
  k= 6: 2,6->P=12
  k= 7: 2,7->P=14, 3,4->P=12
  k= 8: 2,8->P=16
  k= 9: 2,9->P=18, 3,5->P=15
  k=10: 2,10->P=20, 4,4->P=16
  k=11: 2,11->P=22, 3,6->P=18
  k=12: 2,12->P=24
  k=13: 2,13->P=26, 3,7->P=21, 4,5->P=20
  k=14: 2,14->P=28

PRODUCT-SUM CRITICAL PAIRS
========================================================================
For seed F of entries >1, let P=prod(F), S=sum(F), defect D=P-S.
D copies of 1 repair the additive fold: D + S = P.
Total arity is k=|F|+D.  Minimal P by k gives the product-sum number.

k  min_P  compact witness        seed>1        ones  runner_up_Ps
